cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or its retained experimental outputs, please cite the associated anonymous manuscript.
type: software
title: "Beyond Participant-Disjoint Splits: Evaluation Validity for Gait-Based Parkinson's Disease Detection"
authors:
  - name: Anonymous
abstract: >-
  Research software for evaluating participant, preprocessing, and
  training-control independence in gait-based Parkinson's disease detection,
  including deterministic partition replay, an LPGNet factorial protocol
  reconstruction, and separate participant-independent CNN and Mamba benchmarks.
keywords:
  - evaluation validity
  - participant leakage
  - gait classification
  - Parkinson's disease
  - reproducibility
  - nested cross-validation
preferred-citation:
  type: unpublished
  title: "Beyond Participant-Disjoint Splits: Evaluation Validity for Gait-Based Parkinson's Disease Detection"
  authors:
    - name: Anonymous
  year: 2026
  notes: Anonymous manuscript under review at Transactions on Machine Learning Research.
